From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PenguinBurner diagnostics <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 9 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vkd3d: optionally keep Reflex owner with multiple swapchains

This is a diagnostic patch for RE9/PenguinBurner latency testing, not a
general upstream proposal.

Upstream commit 298eaf00 intentionally clears the device
low_latency_swapchain when more than one Vulkan swapchain is live. That is
normally conservative: NVIDIA Reflex has one low-latency swapchain owner per
D3D12 device in this path.

For RE9 debugging we need to distinguish:

1. the game really creates/uses a second swapchain and VKD3D disables Reflex;
2. the NVIDIA timing report ring stalls even while markers and presents still
   advance on the primary swapchain.

Setting VKD3D_LOW_LATENCY_ALLOW_MULTI_SWAPCHAIN=1 keeps the existing
low_latency_swapchain owner instead of clearing it when vk_swapchain_count > 1.
If that makes RE9's gpuRender timing stream survive, the root cause is the
multi-swapchain Reflex guard/ownership path. If it still stalls, the issue is
not solved by keeping the owner alive.
---
 libs/vkd3d/swapchain.c | 21 ++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libs/vkd3d/swapchain.c b/libs/vkd3d/swapchain.c
index 44b59d4d..99d7e8d2 100644
--- a/libs/vkd3d/swapchain.c
+++ b/libs/vkd3d/swapchain.c
@@ -1907,6 +1907,24 @@ static void dxgi_vk_swap_chain_set_low_latency_state(struct dxgi_vk_swap_chain *
     chain->present.low_latency_state = *low_latency_state;
 }
 
+static bool dxgi_vk_swap_chain_allow_multi_swapchain_reflex(void)
+{
+    static bool initialized;
+    static bool enabled;
+    char env[16];
+
+    if (!initialized)
+    {
+        enabled = vkd3d_get_env_var("VKD3D_LOW_LATENCY_ALLOW_MULTI_SWAPCHAIN",
+                env, sizeof(env)) && strcmp(env, "1") == 0;
+        initialized = true;
+        if (enabled)
+            WARN("VKD3D_LOW_LATENCY_ALLOW_MULTI_SWAPCHAIN=1: keeping Reflex low-latency swapchain owner with multiple Vulkan swapchains.\n");
+    }
+
+    return enabled;
+}
+
 static void dxgi_vk_swap_chain_low_latency_state_update(struct dxgi_vk_swap_chain *chain)
 {
     if (chain->request.low_latency_update_requested)
@@ -2288,7 +2306,9 @@ static void dxgi_vk_swap_chain_recreate_swapchain_in_present_task(struct dxgi_vk
         spinlock_acquire(&device->low_latency_swapchain_spinlock);
         device->swapchain_info.vk_swapchain_count++;
 
-        if (device->swapchain_info.vk_swapchain_count > 1 && device->swapchain_info.low_latency_swapchain)
+        if (device->swapchain_info.vk_swapchain_count > 1 &&
+                device->swapchain_info.low_latency_swapchain &&
+                !dxgi_vk_swap_chain_allow_multi_swapchain_reflex())
         {
             dxgi_vk_swap_chain_decref(device->swapchain_info.low_latency_swapchain);
             device->swapchain_info.low_latency_swapchain = NULL;
-- 
